# What never needs to reach the Docker daemon.
#
# This one is not merely a size optimisation — it is a **correctness** fix.
# Both the `development` and `build` stages do `COPY . .` *after* `npm ci` has
# run in the `base` stage, so without this file the host's `node_modules` is
# copied straight over the one the image just installed. That host tree was
# built for the host's platform and may not even be the same architecture.
#
# The dev overlay papers over the symptom with an anonymous `/app/node_modules`
# volume, which is why nobody noticed. The `build` stage has no such volume.
#
# Size: `node_modules` is ~389 MB and `dist` ~9 MB, so this takes a ~399 MB
# context down to under a megabyte.

# Installed by `npm ci` inside the image; never copied in.
node_modules/

# Build output — the `build` stage produces its own.
dist/

# Test and coverage artefacts.
coverage/
__screenshots__/
*.tsbuildinfo

# Local environment overrides must not leak into an image.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

*.log
